{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: implement the adopted trusted-process/single-operator supported-host posture, as the one current-world implementation assignment authorized by coordination request 9d9f3162 (promise 51f0f779). The gate is satisfied: fan-out lane e1ab6474 sealed at de9a2b83 with its verdict published at 12105a30, and the one-base-append lane 95f50368 sealed at 8c0a2052 with the landed behavior documenting the remaining 50 ms budget miss. Historical evidence carried by name and never as bases: adopted decision 8a758fb7, hugh adoption bc758b7a, claude approval 05c1062c, codex review ratification f8542488, design completion 2ff780f2, plus every residual implementation finding from that review. This request rests only on the then-live artifacts covering the scope paths; it deliberately does not rest on historical self-request 3fec5026, the coordination chain, any retired artifact, or any world-stale record, so retiring #2544 cannot stale this assignment.","body":{"conditions":"1) Enforce the adopted trusted-process/single-operator posture without building partial shared-host authentication: choose and name one deliberate per-invocation or explicit named-config operator acknowledgement; fail closed when it is absent; document that it discloses the boundary but does not protect direct gs CLI key access or same-account malware. Resolve every configured listener address and require every result to be loopback; refuse non-loopback. Preserve and test the pre-side-effect Origin, Host, and content-type policy with no permissive CORS path. 2) Replace client-chosen bearer identifiers with resident-minted credentials using at least 128 bits from system cryptographic randomness and a validated opaque form. Bind each credential to exactly one repository and actor; keep the public handle display-only; prevent cross-actor and cross-repository use and replay after departure, non-renewed expiry, restart, or explicit revocation. Preserve the existing global and per-actor session caps, TTL bound, recycled-identifier inbox cleanup, and route-template-only telemetry unless stronger evidence justifies a reviewed change. 3) Remove credential disclosure from presence and ordinary status, MCP whoami and tool results, logs, diagnostics, durable events, referrers, query strings, path segments, returned URL errors, and browser and MCP departure flows, covering both browser UI and MCP clients. Add adversarial tests for guessing, theft and replay, cross-actor and cross-repository confusion, renewal, departure, expiry, restart, revocation, hostile browser origins, malformed credentials, and diagnostics; state plainly that malicious same-account processes remain out of scope. 4) Update startup output, resident status, browser guidance, MCP guidance, deployment and security documentation, and docs/reference/architecture.md in the same exact implementation head. Document the OS account, repository common directory, backups, snapshots, developer tooling, sync and copy paths, compromise response, and the key and capability recovery and rotation boundary; correct the inaccurate internal/custody key-management row; name architecture layers 3 and 7 plus internal/app, and state that kernel verification and fold semantics do not change. 5) Deliver the normal exact-head artifact report and request independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review from claude before merge, including a simplification check that rejects a partial authentication framework which cannot protect against same-account peers. 6) Implement on a request/\u003cslug\u003e branch with per-path artifact succession per the discipline.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}